rawwin(1)

# NAME

rawwin - interactively select an admitted rawm client

# SYNOPSIS

*rawwin*

*rawwin -v*

# DESCRIPTION

*rawwin* is a stateless composition client for interactive managed-window
selection. It obtains rawm's authoritative admitted-client inventory by running
*rawctl clients*, presents those clients through *rawmenu*(1), then requests
focus of the selected XID with *rawctl focus-client*.

rawwin does not enumerate the X window tree, read *\_NET\_CLIENT\_LIST*, send
*\_NET\_ACTIVE\_WINDOW*, or otherwise reconstruct rawm's client authority.
rawm remains responsible for admitting clients and applying focus; rawmenu
remains responsible for selector presentation.

If a selected client disappears while the menu is open, the final *rawctl*
operation fails and rawwin exits unsuccessfully.

# OPTIONS

*-v*, *--version*
	Print the rawwin version and exit.

*-h*, *--help*
	Print usage and exit.

# EXIT STATUS

0
	A client was selected and rawm confirmed the requested focus.

1
	The inventory could not be obtained or parsed, no clients were admitted,
	the menu was cancelled or failed, the selection was malformed, or rawm
	rejected the final focus request.

# SEE ALSO

*rawctl*(1), *rawmenu*(1), *rawm*(1)
